experimental/gittuf: verify, load, and author policy over any Storer

Repository is bound to an on-disk Git repository, so a caller with its
own storage backend cannot reach the policy engine through it.

StorerRepository wraps any gitstore.Storer and carries the operations
that need nothing more. VerifyRef and VerifyRefFromEntry return the tip
the RSL attests instead of comparing it with the store's current ref,
so a caller can verify a tip it has not installed yet. Unlike
Repository.VerifyRefFromEntry, the latter is not gated on dev mode.

LoadPolicy loads and verifies the applied policy. It reads the RSL tip
once and uses it throughout, takes WithEntry to load one policy entry,
and WithInitialRootKeys to anchor the first root. The returned Policy
reports its root's version and key IDs, lists every principal it
declares, and answers through Satisfies whether a set of principals
meets the policy for a reference, using the engine's own rule
selection and thresholds.

AuthorPolicy signs a root and a top-level rule file from crypto.Signer
and crypto.PublicKey values and writes only the policy tree. The caller
commits it and records the update. The authored state must pass
State.Verify before it is written.

Repository.VerifyRef now shares its verifier selection with
StorerRepository.VerifyRef.

